# Where the caged Thomas may connect through the network fence (scripts/cage/egress_proxy.py).
# enable_network_fence.ps1 copies this into C:\ProgramData\ThomasPins\egress.allow, which
# only an administrator can change; editing this repo copy changes nothing until that
# script runs again at a UAC prompt. One host per line; "*.name" allows its subdomains.

# Model providers: the hosts thomas.toml configures, and the Codex sign-in refresh.
chatgpt.com
auth.openai.com
api.openai.com
api.anthropic.com
generativelanguage.googleapis.com
openrouter.ai
api.mistral.ai
api.groq.com
api.together.xyz
api.deepinfra.com
api.fireworks.ai
api.x.ai
api.cerebras.ai
api.perplexity.ai
open.bigmodel.cn

# The Claude CLI's sign-in refresh, measured 2026-09-24 (Claude Code 2.1.278, nonessential
# traffic off): with an expired sign-in it opened CONNECT platform.claude.com:443, then
# api.anthropic.com:443 (already above); with a current one, api.anthropic.com only.
# The fence works per host, so this makes the whole platform.claude.com host (the
# Anthropic Console) reachable from the cage, not only its /v1/oauth/token path.
platform.claude.com

# Package installs inside caged tasks.
pypi.org
files.pythonhosted.org
registry.npmjs.org
